AdvantagesThe Prototype pattern improves performance and flexibility in object creation.Reduces costly object initialization by cloning existing objects using a clone() method.Simplifies object creation and minimizes the need for multiple subclasses for different configurations.Allows flexible modification of cloned objects and supports dynamic addition or removal of object types.Improves performance and flexibility in object creation.Disadvantages Although efficient, the Prototype pattern introduces certain challenges.Cloning complex objects can be difficult.Deep copy implementation can be complicated.Requires careful handling of references to avoid shared state issues.Every class must implement cloning logic properly.
